From 0c8d02b220bc55ede0aa7f17181627db1ca4ac27 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kryxzort <101042137+Kryxzort@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 14:18:54 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 59/81] render: compile effect shaders as leniently as WE's
 HLSL path
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Workshop effects are written against WE's compiler, which accepts what GLSL 3.30 refuses. Four of them, all
in 3414858021's compose layer (the one holding the girl's head, eyes and hair, with the deformer_simulation
and iris_movement__ effects), made the layer fail to build, so nothing under it was drawn:

- a backslash at the end of a line continues it (depthparallax.frag splits an expression over two lines;
  glslang splices only from GLSL 4.20) — spliced before parsing, the lines put back after the joined one so
  error line numbers still match;
- a fragment unit may assign to its varyings (depthparallax.frag: `v_Depth += …`; HLSL inputs are plain
  parameters) — such a varying is read into a global copy at the top of main, its other uses go to the copy;
- a wider float vector with a narrower one truncates to the narrower (iris_movement__.vert:
  `vec2 da = transformedCursorPosition * g_CursorScale`, a vec4 times a vec2) — from glslang's "wrong operand
  types" / "cannot convert" error, the line's variables declared with the wider type take the narrower
  swizzle and the unit is parsed again (at most 16 times);
- an #endif with no #if is dropped (iris_movement__.vert has a stray one after its FOLLOWCURSOR block).

Origin: ours
Why: docs/player/spikes/we-lwe-gap-audit.md, 3414858021 result
Status: candidate-for-upstream
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
